#: src/development/windows.md:121
msgid "Troubleshooting"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/windows.md:123
msgid "Setting `RUSTFLAGS` env var breaks builds"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/windows.md:125
msgid ""
"If you set the `RUSTFLAGS` env var, it will override the `rustflags` "
"settings in `.cargo/config.toml` which is required to properly build Zed."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/windows.md:127
msgid ""
"Because these settings change over time, the resulting build errors may vary "
"from linker failures to other hard-to-diagnose errors."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/windows.md:129
msgid ""
"If you need extra Rust flags, use one of the following approaches in `.cargo/"
"config.toml`:"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/windows.md:131
msgid "Add your flags in the build section"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/windows.md:133
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"[build]\n"
"rustflags = [\"-C\", \"symbol-mangling-version=v0\", \"--cfg\", "
"\"tokio_unstable\"]\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/windows.md:138
msgid "Add your flags in the windows target section"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/windows.md:140
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"[target.'cfg(target_os = \"windows\")']\n"
"rustflags = [\n"
"    \"--cfg\",\n"
"    \"windows_slim_errors\",\n"
"    \"-C\",\n"
"    \"target-feature=+crt-static\",\n"
"]\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/windows.md:150
msgid ""
"Or, create a new `.cargo/config.toml` in the parent directory of the Zed "
"repo (see below). This is useful in CI because you do not need to edit the "
"repo's original `.cargo/config.toml`."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/windows.md:152
msgid ""
"```\n"
"upper_dir\n"
"├── .cargo          // <-- Make this folder\n"
"│   └── config.toml // <-- Make this file\n"
"└── zed\n"
"    ├── .cargo\n"
"    │   └── config.toml\n"
"    └── crates\n"
"        ├── assistant\n"
"        └── ...\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/windows.md:164
msgid ""
"In the new (above) `.cargo/config.toml`, if we wanted to add `--cfg gles` to "
"our rustflags, it would look like this"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/windows.md:166
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"[target.'cfg(all())']\n"
"rustflags = [\"--cfg\", \"gles\"]\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/windows.md:171
msgid "Cargo errors claiming that a dependency is using unstable features"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/windows.md:173
msgid "Try `cargo clean` and `cargo build`."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/windows.md:175
msgid "`STATUS_ACCESS_VIOLATION`"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/windows.md:177
msgid ""
"This error can happen if you are using the \"rust-lld.exe\" linker. Consider "
"trying a different linker."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/windows.md:179
msgid ""
"If you are using a global config, consider moving the Zed repository to a "
"nested directory and add a `.cargo/config.toml` with a custom linker config "
"in the parent directory."
msgstr ""

